# The partition's retired floor is checked on every stamped append, as revision 4
# specified, through the append admission predicate. The floor is one value per
# partition but epochs are per leaf, so after another leaf's retirement a live
# leaf's append is refused although nothing superseded it (#5635).
MODULE: OnlySupersededRefusedFloorAtAppend
TARGET: OnlySupersededRefused
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: the append admission predicate also checks the partition's retired floor
PERTURBS: OwnAlloc, StaleAppend
BOUNDS: WithOtherRetire = TRUE, Ghosts = TRUE, WithBatch = FALSE, MaxWindows = 1

--- FIND
AppendAdmits(a) == epoch[a] >= memFence
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the partition's retired floor is checked on the append path too.
AppendAdmits(a) == epoch[a] >= memFence /\ epoch[a] > retired
--- END